silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_5__step_y_stability__homcatus__mittens_=_empty_now_=>_homcatus__mitt a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, a negative-regression claim is stable: if Hom(catus, Mittens) is empty now, the naturality of the profile transformation says it remains empty unless a new arrow from catus to Mittens is explicitly added to O_01. No future agent can silently re-introduce the catus-Mittens identity collapse; they would have to add an explicit arrow, which would fire the regression test R1." .
